a component doubled in the result, a => a^a: einsum spec "a => a^a": the component a appears twice in the concatenated axis a^a, but a segment is one range of positions with one index, so only one of its copies would be read or written. To repeat a tensor along an axis, pass it once per copy under distinct components: (x, x) ++^ "a; b => a^b"
